        "Infatuated with their military might, the chieftains of 'Ad replied with insolent pride: ﴿فَأَمَّا عَادٌ فَاسْتَكْبَرُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ بِغَيْرِ الْحَقِّ وَقَالُوا مَنْ أَشَدُّ مِنَّا قُوَّةً﴾ 'As for 'Ad, they were arrogant upon the earth without right and said, \"Who is greater than us in strength?\"' (Surah Fussilat 41:15). They accused Hud of foolishness and dared him to unleash the promised divine punishment.",
        "Divine retribution commenced with an agonizing three-year drought. Desperate for water, the people of 'Ad looked toward the sky and rejoiced when they saw dense black clouds approaching their mountains: ﴿فَلَمَّا رَأَوْهُ عَارِضًا مُّسْتَقْبِلَ أَوْدِيَتِهِمْ قَالُوا هَٰذَا عَارِضٌ مُّمْطِرُنَا﴾ 'And when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys, they said, \"This is a cloud bringing us rain!\"' But Prophet Hud declared: ﴿بَلْ هُوَ مَا اسْتَعْجَلْتُم بِهِ رِيحٌ فِيهَا عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ﴾ 'Nay, it is that which you were asking to be hastened—a wind wherein is a painful punishment!' (Surah Al-Ahqaf 46:24).",
        "That dark cloud unleashed a furious, sub-zero gale that howled relentlessly for seven nights and eight continuous days: ﴿سَخَّرَهَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَبْعَ لَيَالٍ وَثَمَانِيَةَ أَيَّامٍ حُسُومًا فَتَرَى الْقَوْمَ فِيهَا صَرْعَىٰ كَأَنَّهُمْ أَعْجَازُ نَخْلٍ خَاوِيَةٍ﴾ 'Which Allah subjected upon them for seven nights and eight days in succession, so you would see the people therein fallen as if they were hollow trunks of palm trees.' (Surah Al-Haqqah 69:7). The violent wind lifted giant warriors into the air and dashed their skulls upon the rocks, burying their proud towers under shifting desert sands.",
